00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:07.180
and then you get a piece of paper

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.820
that says 'You're ready for the world.'

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:09.640
uh-

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.000
But what it doesn't teach you is

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.960
that the world is what you make of it

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.580
like, even if you're going into college,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.760
Try hobbies.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.760
Join clubs.

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:17.900
Meet people.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:20.600
Meeting people is probably the best skill

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.960
that you could possibly ever learn

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.760
and you gotta do it with baby steps

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.740
by taking it very slow.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.480
And I went to college after high school,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.540
I didn't take those steps

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.400
to go out and push my comfort zone out.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.340
It wasn't until after college

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.980
that I really started to find who I was

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.080
when I started doing 
YouTube.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.180
Becauce I continually tried to do new things.

